{"id": "EUVD-2026-95123", "enisaUuid": "467eaa86-cdbf-3f96-bf3e-05ca5f9d09cd", "description": "FFmpeg before 8.1.3 contains an infinite loop vulnerability in the HLS demuxer that allows remote attackers to cause denial of service because parse_playlist() accepts Master Playlist tags inside Media Playlists. Attackers can trick victims into opening a crafted self-referencing playlist that endlessly adds variants in hls_read_header(), causing unbounded CPU and I/O consumption.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T17:30:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T01:03:34", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/c364ab176f722bdabc886845e770c9eacbc1e3e5", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/0e6eef35517a", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/a4ddaba8bb78", "https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/23618", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n8.1.2/libavformat/hls.c#L866", "https://gist.github.com/OxBat/59574a2940092cda1b6e76bbf96f53d0", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-before-8.1.3-hls-demuxer-infinite-loop-via-self-referencing-playlist"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wrmh-p2hh-7cf6", "CVE-2026-107695"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "65948b61-642c-3435-8078-7e042ecb9c41", "product": {"name": "FFmpeg", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}, "product_version": "0 <8.1.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0bef24a6-cb69-347c-b1ab-dd087c133678", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}], "isExploited": false}